<title>USA: DIGEX to offer more shares in IPO.</title>
<headline>DIGEX to offer more shares in IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>DIGEX Inc raised the number of shares to be offered in its inital public offering to 4.5 million from its prior estimate of 3.75 million, according to a regulatory filing.</p>
<p>The company will offer the shares in an estimated range of $9 to $11. Friedman Billings Ramsay, the lead underwriter of the offering, said the deal is tentatively scheduled to price tonight for trading tomorrow.</p>
<p>Analysts have said they expect the Washington, D.C.-based Internet carrier to fetch solid premiums.</p>
</text>
